---
import WysPhoto from './WysPhoto.astro';
import {examples} from '../data/wys.js';
---
<section class="wys-wrap wys-section">
 <div class="wx-centered"><p class="wys-label">A closer look at the handoff</p><h2>The input is specific.<br/><em>The next step is clear.</em></h2><p>Here is a sanitized worksheet for the Pretty Wicked example. It shows how the look stays connected through the workflow.</p></div>
 <div class="wx-worksheet"><WysPhoto photo={examples[0].photos[0]} treatment="double" label="Pretty Wicked / the starting point"/><div class="wx-worksheet-paper"><span class="wx-file-label">LOOK BRIEF / WORKED EXAMPLE</span><dl><div><dt>Theme & category</dt><dd>Pink Halloween · Home Decor · Entryway</dd></div><div><dt>Selected products</dt><dd>Five recorded types: pumpkins, gauze, string lights, bats and LED tea lights.</dd></div><div><dt>The three photo jobs</dt><dd>Overhead pieces → no-person styled console → distinct porch-door lifestyle moment.</dd></div><div><dt>Output plan</dt><dd>3 photos, 3 Pins, 3 carousel slides, 1 article, product notes and channel copy.</dd></div><div><dt>Destination path</dt><dd>The actual Lifestyle article is available. Per-look affiliate links and Amazon list submission remain pending.</dd></div><div><dt>Saved next action</dt><dd>Verify the selected products and exact shopping destinations before any social publishing.</dd></div></dl><div class="wx-checkpoint"><b>A checkpoint, not a restart.</b><p>Accepted photographs and the article stay attached to the same look. Pending destinations do not erase the completed content or silently become verified.</p></div></div></div>
</section>
